<unit id="abb10387-4701-42c2-9e13-280e41fd8408">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 2</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: # </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVIDIA Monitor</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="3f26e1cc-fade-4d87-bab2-62359514ac00">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 4</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on allows you to monitor various parameters of NVIDIA graphics cards, such as name, used memory, free and total memory, power usage, temperature, and more.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="5eabfbe3-5ec7-46e9-b76c-ce246069ae8a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 6</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Shortcuts</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="15d19137-50ae-421d-be79-d7f7d849ea92">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 8</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Note: Some information parameters may not be compatible or supported depending on the graphics card.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="e1bed0f6-7e19-4769-9f93-3d98207de900">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 9</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>All the following shortcuts can be customized in the input gestures/NVIDIAMonitor category. Pressing a shortcut twice copies the information to the clipboard.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8f1eeddc-a1a7-4f96-9a17-b7686d4c3260">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 11</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + g: Announces the GPU name/model.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="52cdb5a0-8793-470e-8694-1ad27adee29f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 12</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + u: Announces the GPU UUID.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d1aba7bd-6be2-4819-9dea-3c06646028b5">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 13</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + v: Announces the driver version.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="426b20ab-f4ed-4c6a-82f4-ece484d454fc">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 14</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + v: Announces the BIOS version.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f4b21a72-82f8-4408-a4f0-4dda884fccc4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 15</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 1: Announces the GPU load.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7a806a73-f8d6-4712-96df-68ddbce9099c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 16</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 2: Announces the memory load.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="150d4c94-39f0-41b7-9989-1ae20ed856b2">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 17</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 3: Announces the free memory.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8665a205-1ad4-4544-89d0-656a8cace532">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 18</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 4: Announces the used memory.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="629cb9f1-33fa-4cbf-99e0-85d85b3d5501">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 19</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 5: Announces the total memory.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0cf96c36-7d7c-4a70-a448-1aa2d4b50c2a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 20</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 6: Announces the GPU temperature.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c28e7709-0943-49b7-ab89-adac64633e6e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 21</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 7: Announces the power consumption.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="510794c9-5d79-4769-867f-62ccfce78028">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 22</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 8: Announces the power limit.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="bb1d8792-2f1f-4323-bb04-64609e909cde">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 23</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 9: Announces the number of CUDA processes.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="017d0a74-693b-4a29-a4ef-8e46a538d6bd">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 24</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + alt + 0: Announces the memory used by processes.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ca11d9ce-4b64-4e28-b643-50448ae68dde">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 25</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 1: Announces the fan speed.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="3015a455-8f6e-4f7c-8db9-8873213fb0e9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 26</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 2: Announces the GPU clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="597d0a8d-f94c-4104-9bef-6e75e94b5812">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 27</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 3: Announces the maximum GPU clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c5c12d32-5793-46b1-8ae5-15bdc25fe8be">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 28</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 4: Announces the SM clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="57c51b01-805f-445f-8494-4ba06987d6cd">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 29</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 5: Announces the maximum SM clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="bfafa260-a7e7-48da-9e5e-4c352f239f90">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 30</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 6: Announces the memory clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2bb63228-a76d-4b41-959d-8228fdd30daf">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 31</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 7: Announces the maximum memory clock frequency.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2eb12217-bf75-43b8-a6a3-40e1f4efd236">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 32</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 8: Announces the TX throughput.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d9251fbc-fe04-4baa-894e-ca8b4ee800c5">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 33</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 9: Announces the RX throughput.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="5253bbdf-ae62-4d4a-9f88-0f8c19baa1c9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 34</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>- NVDA + ctrl + alt + 0: Announces the power state.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
